    "created_at": "2024-10-30T17:52:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-10-30T17:57:00Z",
    "body": "> allow any element to have a custom element as a parent.\r\n\r\nSounds OK, but the custom parent element would need to have a role that allows `role=\"listitem\"` or `role=\"option\"` as children no? Unless the `<option>` or `<li>` default roles are overwritten by an explicit role.\r\n\r\nfrom ARIA 1.3 editors draft: https://w3c.github.io/aria/\r\n\r\n> Authors MUST ensure [elements](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element) whose [role](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#dfn-role) is listitem are [accessibility children](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#dfn-accessibility-child) of an [element](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element) whose [role](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#dfn-role) is [list](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#list).\r\n\r\n> Authors MUST ensure [elements](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-element) with [role](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#dfn-role) option are [accessibility children](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#dfn-accessibility-child) of an element with [role](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#dfn-role) [listbox](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#listbox) or of an element with [role](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#dfn-role) [group](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#group) that is the [accessibility child](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#dfn-accessibility-child) of an element with [role](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#dfn-role) listbox. Options not associated with a [listbox](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#listbox) might not be correctly mapped to an [accessibility API](https://w3c.github.io/aria/#dfn-accessibility-api).",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
